  "body": "<!-- THESIS: The user-selected studies form one connected Mycelium, with learning and community equally prominent.\nOWN-WORLD: Soil brown, forest, cool sage and stone; bold Manrope; photographic layers, plant sculpture and clear library controls.\nSTORY: Discover permaculture, find a starting point, and connect with others on Common Ground.\nFIRST VIEWPORT: Farm's seedling and large headline at home; panoramic type on About; big left-aligned titles and layered media in libraries. Equal learning/community actions remain on home.\nFORM: User-selected Farm-to-Fauna composition, Interstellar About and study-derived libraries. Selection key: mycelium-selected-studies-2026-10-16.\nFINISH: unreviewed and undocumented is unfinished; this build ends with the finish review, the verdict, and DESIGN.md --><a class=\"skip-link\" href=\"#main\">Skip to content</a>\n<header class=\"site-header\"><a aria-label=\"Mycelium home\" class=\"brand\" href=\"/\"><img alt=\"Mycelium\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"88\" loading=\"eager\" sizes=\"230px\" src=\"/redesign/delivery/media/d6b5b92b-logo-be405390b89c-400.webp\" srcset=\"/redesign/delivery/media/d6b5b92b-logo-be405390b89c-320.webp 320w, /redesign/delivery/media/d6b5b92b-logo-be405390b89c-400.webp 400w\" width=\"400\"/></a><button aria-controls=\"site-menu\" aria-expanded=\"false\" class=\"menu-button\"><span>Menu</span><i aria-hidden=\"true\"></i></button></header>\n<nav aria-label=\"Main navigation\" class=\"site-menu\" hidden=\"\" id=\"site-menu\"><div class=\"menu-links\"><a class=\"menu-route\" href=\"/videos/\"><span>Videos</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 12h16M13 5l7 7-7 7\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></path></svg></a><a class=\"menu-route\" href=\"/courses/\"><span>Courses</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 12h16M13 5l7 7-7 7\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></path></svg></a><a class=\"menu-route\" href=\"/common-ground/\"><span>Forum</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 12h16M13 5l7 7-7 7\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></path></svg></a><a class=\"menu-route\" href=\"/resources/\"><span>Resources</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 12h16M13 5l7 7-7 7\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></path></svg></a><a class=\"menu-route\" href=\"/about/\"><span>My story</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 12h16M13 5l7 7-7 7\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></path></svg></a></div><div class=\"menu-bottom\"><a href=\"/\">Home</a><a class=\"footer-link\" href=\"/events/\"><span>Events</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 12h16M13 5l7 7-7 7\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></path></svg></a><a class=\"footer-link\" href=\"/newsletter/\"><span>Newsletter</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 12h16M13 5l7 7-7 7\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></path></svg></a><a class=\"footer-link\" href=\"/feedback/\"><span>Get in touch</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 12h16M13 5l7 7-7 7\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></path></svg></a></div></nav><main id=\"main\"><section class=\"archive-intro\"><div><a class=\"text-link\" href=\"/events/\"><span>Back to events</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 12h16M13 5l7 7-7 7\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></path></svg></a><h1>Event <span>archive.</span></h1><p>Gatherings end.<br/>The ideas keep growing.</p></div><div class=\"archive-intro-note\"><span>WORKSHOPS · TALKS · COURSES</span><p>Revisit five past gatherings from our community. Explore the details, follow a story, take something with you.</p></div></section><section aria-label=\"Past gatherings\" class=\"event-archive-section\"><div class=\"archive-stories\"><article class=\"archive-story\" data-archive-story=\"\" id=\"kabuohan\"><div class=\"archive-object\" data-object-scene=\"\"><span class=\"object-index\">01 / 05</span><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"object-plinth\"></div><model-viewer alt=\"A handmade clay bowl with a growing seedling\" auto-rotate-delay=\"0\" camera-orbit=\"25deg 65deg 105%\" data-archive-model=\"\" data-model-src=\"/redesign/delivery/media/clay-b66301c2548e.glb\" exposure=\".9\" field-of-view=\"30deg\" interaction-prompt=\"none\" loading=\"lazy\" reveal=\"auto\" rotation-per-second=\"35deg\" shadow-intensity=\"1\" shadow-softness=\"1\" tabindex=\"-1\"><span slot=\"progress-bar\"></span><img alt=\"A handmade clay bowl with a growing seedling\" class=\"object-poster\" data-lazy-media=\"\" data-src=\"/redesign/delivery/media/clay-9cfc3c45d4b4-640.webp\" data-srcset=\"/redesign/delivery/media/clay-9cfc3c45d4b4-320.webp 320w, /redesign/delivery/media/clay-9cfc3c45d4b4-640.webp 640w\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"640\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 700px) 90vw, (max-width: 1100px) 50vw, 35vw\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAAD/ACwAAAAAAQABAAACADs=\" width=\"640\"/><noscript><img alt=\"A handmade clay bowl with a growing seedling\" class=\"object-poster\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"640\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 700px) 90vw, (max-width: 1100px) 50vw, 35vw\" src=\"/redesign/delivery/media/clay-9cfc3c45d4b4-640.webp\" srcset=\"/redesign/delivery/media/clay-9cfc3c45d4b4-320.webp 320w, /redesign/delivery/media/clay-9cfc3c45d4b4-640.webp 640w\" width=\"640\"/></noscript></model-viewer><button aria-label=\"Rotate sculpture: Kabuohan Workshop\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"object-spin\" data-object-spin=\"\" type=\"button\">Turn it around <span aria-hidden=\"true\">↻</span></button><span class=\"object-type\">Workshop / 2026</span></div><div class=\"archive-copy\"><div class=\"archive-meta\"><span>25 JUN 2026</span><span>Workshop · Rizal Art House</span></div><h2>Kabuohan Workshop</h2><p class=\"archive-host\">Baganihan Collective</p><p class=\"archive-preview\">A day of permaculture gardening and primitive pottery for homeschool families at Rizal Art House.</p><details><summary>Inside the workshop<span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary><div class=\"archive-details\"><p>Permaculture gardening and primitive pottery for homeschool families, facilitated by Hubert Posadas at Rizal Art House.</p><p>The published recap follows a day of sensory observation, food-forest design, building a hugelkultur bed and working with clay.</p><p class=\"archive-closed\">This event has passed. Registration is closed.</p><a class=\"text-link\" href=\"/events/kabuohan-workshop/\"><span>Read the full workshop story</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 12h16M13 5l7 7-7 7\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></path></svg></a></div></details></div></article><article class=\"archive-story\" data-archive-story=\"\" id=\"disruption\"><div class=\"archive-object\" data-object-scene=\"\"><span class=\"object-index\">02 / 05</span><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"object-plinth\"></div><model-viewer alt=\"A connected landscape with a pond, rainwater vessel, community shelter, trees and garden beds\" auto-rotate-delay=\"0\" camera-orbit=\"25deg 65deg 105%\" data-archive-model=\"\" data-model-src=\"/redesign/delivery/media/water-ab2982cf4e3d.glb\" exposure=\".9\" field-of-view=\"30deg\" interaction-prompt=\"none\" loading=\"lazy\" reveal=\"auto\" rotation-per-second=\"35deg\" shadow-intensity=\"1\" shadow-softness=\"1\" tabindex=\"-1\"><span slot=\"progress-bar\"></span><img alt=\"A connected landscape with a pond, rainwater vessel, community shelter, trees and garden beds\" class=\"object-poster\" data-lazy-media=\"\" data-src=\"/redesign/delivery/media/water-cb8fe422ce34-640.webp\" data-srcset=\"/redesign/delivery/media/water-cb8fe422ce34-320.webp 320w, /redesign/delivery/media/water-cb8fe422ce34-640.webp 640w, /redesign/delivery/media/water-cb8fe422ce34-900.webp 900w\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"900\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 700px) 90vw, (max-width: 1100px) 50vw, 35vw\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAAD/ACwAAAAAAQABAAACADs=\" width=\"900\"/><noscript><img alt=\"A connected landscape with a pond, rainwater vessel, community shelter, trees and garden beds\" class=\"object-poster\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"900\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 700px) 90vw, (max-width: 1100px) 50vw, 35vw\" src=\"/redesign/delivery/media/water-cb8fe422ce34-640.webp\" srcset=\"/redesign/delivery/media/water-cb8fe422ce34-320.webp 320w, /redesign/delivery/media/water-cb8fe422ce34-640.webp 640w, /redesign/delivery/media/water-cb8fe422ce34-900.webp 900w\" width=\"900\"/></noscript></model-viewer><button aria-label=\"Rotate sculpture: Permanent Culture in Times of Disruption: Why Permaculturists Need to Think Beyond Food\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"object-spin\" data-object-spin=\"\" type=\"button\">Turn it around <span aria-hidden=\"true\">↻</span></button><span class=\"object-type\">Talk / 2026</span></div><div class=\"archive-copy\"><div class=\"archive-meta\"><span>26 JUN 2026 · 8 PM PHT</span><span>Talk · Online</span></div><h2>Permanent Culture in Times of Disruption: Why Permaculturists Need to Think Beyond Food</h2><p class=\"archive-host\">Baganihan Collective</p><p class=\"archive-preview\">Thinking beyond food: risk, mutual aid and the systems that help communities navigate disruption.</p><details><summary>About this past event<span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary><div class=\"archive-details\"><p>Permaculture gives us powerful tools for food security and ecological resilience — but communities don't survive crises through agriculture alone. This talk explores risk management, mutual aid, physical security, and indigenous practices as essential dimensions of permanent culture.</p><p>Hubert Posadas is a Permaculture Aid Specialist and Risk and Community Security Practitioner with deep experience in community preparedness, mutual aid systems, and indigenous approaches to resilience. He serves as Convenor of the Baganihan Collective, where he works at the intersection of permaculture design and community protection.</p><p class=\"archive-closed\">This event has passed. Registration is closed.</p><a class=\"text-link\" href=\"/events/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Original event listing ↗<span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></div></details></div></article><article class=\"archive-story\" data-archive-story=\"\" id=\"design-course\"><div class=\"archive-object\" data-object-scene=\"\"><span class=\"object-index\">03 / 05</span><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"object-plinth\"></div><model-viewer alt=\"A miniature terraced food forest\" auto-rotate-delay=\"0\" camera-orbit=\"25deg 65deg 105%\" data-archive-model=\"\" data-model-src=\"/redesign/delivery/media/terraces-dd4dda6a8f7b.glb\" exposure=\".9\" field-of-view=\"30deg\" interaction-prompt=\"none\" loading=\"lazy\" reveal=\"auto\" rotation-per-second=\"35deg\" shadow-intensity=\"1\" shadow-softness=\"1\" tabindex=\"-1\"><span slot=\"progress-bar\"></span><img alt=\"A miniature terraced food forest\" class=\"object-poster\" data-lazy-media=\"\" data-src=\"/redesign/delivery/media/terraces-a68b1970526d-640.webp\" data-srcset=\"/redesign/delivery/media/terraces-a68b1970526d-320.webp 320w, /redesign/delivery/media/terraces-a68b1970526d-640.webp 640w\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"640\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 700px) 90vw, (max-width: 1100px) 50vw, 35vw\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAAD/ACwAAAAAAQABAAACADs=\" width=\"640\"/><noscript><img alt=\"A miniature terraced food forest\" class=\"object-poster\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"640\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 700px) 90vw, (max-width: 1100px) 50vw, 35vw\" src=\"/redesign/delivery/media/terraces-a68b1970526d-640.webp\" srcset=\"/redesign/delivery/media/terraces-a68b1970526d-320.webp 320w, /redesign/delivery/media/terraces-a68b1970526d-640.webp 640w\" width=\"640\"/></noscript></model-viewer><button aria-label=\"Rotate sculpture: Basic Permaculture Design Course\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"object-spin\" data-object-spin=\"\" type=\"button\">Turn it around <span aria-hidden=\"true\">↻</span></button><span class=\"object-type\">Course / 2026</span></div><div class=\"archive-copy\"><div class=\"archive-meta\"><span>04–10 JUL 2026</span><span>Course · Nueva Ecija</span></div><h2>Basic Permaculture Design Course</h2><p class=\"archive-host\">Philippine Permaculture Association</p><p class=\"archive-preview\">Seven days exploring sustainable farming, natural systems and resilient living in Nueva Ecija.</p><details><summary>About this past event<span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary><div class=\"archive-details\"><p>Discover practical ways to create a regenerative, eco-friendly lifestyle. Open to farmers, students, gardeners, entrepreneurs, and anyone curious about sustainable living.</p><p>A seven-day, paid, in-person course at Ecodee Permaculture Research Institute, Nueva Ecija.</p><p>The published programme covered sustainable farming, hands-on workshops, natural systems and resilient living.</p><p class=\"archive-closed\">This event has passed. Registration is closed.</p><a class=\"text-link\" href=\"/events/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Original event listing ↗<span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></div></details></div></article><article class=\"archive-story\" data-archive-story=\"\" id=\"seed-sovereignty\"><div class=\"archive-object\" data-object-scene=\"\"><span class=\"object-index\">04 / 05</span><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"object-plinth\"></div><model-viewer alt=\"A seed-keeping collection with heirloom beans, grain heads, packets and an open pod\" auto-rotate-delay=\"0\" camera-orbit=\"25deg 65deg 105%\" data-archive-model=\"\" data-model-src=\"/redesign/delivery/media/seeds-fe009484b1b2.glb\" exposure=\".9\" field-of-view=\"30deg\" interaction-prompt=\"none\" loading=\"lazy\" reveal=\"auto\" rotation-per-second=\"35deg\" shadow-intensity=\"1\" shadow-softness=\"1\" tabindex=\"-1\"><span slot=\"progress-bar\"></span><img alt=\"A seed-keeping collection with heirloom beans, grain heads, packets and an open pod\" class=\"object-poster\" data-lazy-media=\"\" data-src=\"/redesign/delivery/media/seeds-17a36083e16c-640.webp\" data-srcset=\"/redesign/delivery/media/seeds-17a36083e16c-320.webp 320w, /redesign/delivery/media/seeds-17a36083e16c-640.webp 640w, /redesign/delivery/media/seeds-17a36083e16c-900.webp 900w\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"900\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 700px) 90vw, (max-width: 1100px) 50vw, 35vw\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAAD/ACwAAAAAAQABAAACADs=\" width=\"900\"/><noscript><img alt=\"A seed-keeping collection with heirloom beans, grain heads, packets and an open pod\" class=\"object-poster\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"900\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 700px) 90vw, (max-width: 1100px) 50vw, 35vw\" src=\"/redesign/delivery/media/seeds-17a36083e16c-640.webp\" srcset=\"/redesign/delivery/media/seeds-17a36083e16c-320.webp 320w, /redesign/delivery/media/seeds-17a36083e16c-640.webp 640w, /redesign/delivery/media/seeds-17a36083e16c-900.webp 900w\" width=\"900\"/></noscript></model-viewer><button aria-label=\"Rotate sculpture: A Talk on the Importance and Need for Seed Sovereignty\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"object-spin\" data-object-spin=\"\" type=\"button\">Turn it around <span aria-hidden=\"true\">↻</span></button><span class=\"object-type\">Talk / 2026</span></div><div class=\"archive-copy\"><div class=\"archive-meta\"><span>23 MAY 2026 · 8 PM PHT</span><span>Talk · Online</span></div><h2>A Talk on the Importance and Need for Seed Sovereignty</h2><p class=\"archive-host\">Baganihan Collective</p><p class=\"archive-preview\">Lee of ethic explores seeds, cultural memory and the communities working to protect them.</p><details><summary>About this past event<span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary><div class=\"archive-details\"><p>A graduate of the Rocky Mountain Seed Alliance Seed School Teacher Training (2018), Lee has spent years working across Southeast and South Asia's grassroots seed networks — from indigenous communities in militarized zones to UN-level policy spaces advocating for seed commons and farmer rights. Founder of ethic (Earth, Technology, Human Inspired Collaborations), a Global South initiative working at the intersection of ecological intelligence, technology governance, and community sovereignty. An engineer, poet, artist, and musician — Lee teaches not just the science of seeds, but their cultural memory and the politics of who gets to hold them.</p><p class=\"archive-closed\">This event has passed. Registration is closed.</p><a class=\"text-link\" href=\"/events/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Original event listing ↗<span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></div></details></div></article><article class=\"archive-story\" data-archive-story=\"\" id=\"ancestral-wisdom\"><div class=\"archive-object\" data-object-scene=\"\"><span class=\"object-index\">05 / 05</span><div aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"object-plinth\"></div><model-viewer alt=\"A mature tree with branching roots, young plants and a fallen log returning to the soil\" auto-rotate-delay=\"0\" camera-orbit=\"25deg 65deg 105%\" data-archive-model=\"\" data-model-src=\"/redesign/delivery/media/branch-7363673f1145.glb\" exposure=\".9\" field-of-view=\"30deg\" interaction-prompt=\"none\" loading=\"lazy\" reveal=\"auto\" rotation-per-second=\"35deg\" shadow-intensity=\"1\" shadow-softness=\"1\" tabindex=\"-1\"><span slot=\"progress-bar\"></span><img alt=\"A mature tree with branching roots, young plants and a fallen log returning to the soil\" class=\"object-poster\" data-lazy-media=\"\" data-src=\"/redesign/delivery/media/branch-51b7fa31b56a-640.webp\" data-srcset=\"/redesign/delivery/media/branch-51b7fa31b56a-320.webp 320w, /redesign/delivery/media/branch-51b7fa31b56a-640.webp 640w, /redesign/delivery/media/branch-51b7fa31b56a-900.webp 900w\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"900\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 700px) 90vw, (max-width: 1100px) 50vw, 35vw\" src=\"data:image/gif;base64,R0lGODlhAQABAAD/ACwAAAAAAQABAAACADs=\" width=\"900\"/><noscript><img alt=\"A mature tree with branching roots, young plants and a fallen log returning to the soil\" class=\"object-poster\" decoding=\"async\" height=\"900\" loading=\"lazy\" sizes=\"(max-width: 700px) 90vw, (max-width: 1100px) 50vw, 35vw\" src=\"/redesign/delivery/media/branch-51b7fa31b56a-640.webp\" srcset=\"/redesign/delivery/media/branch-51b7fa31b56a-320.webp 320w, /redesign/delivery/media/branch-51b7fa31b56a-640.webp 640w, /redesign/delivery/media/branch-51b7fa31b56a-900.webp 900w\" width=\"900\"/></noscript></model-viewer><button aria-label=\"Rotate sculpture: Ancestral Wisdom in Modern Times: Indigenous Peoples as Guardians of Sustainable Ecosystems\" aria-pressed=\"false\" class=\"object-spin\" data-object-spin=\"\" type=\"button\">Turn it around <span aria-hidden=\"true\">↻</span></button><span class=\"object-type\">Talk / 2026</span></div><div class=\"archive-copy\"><div class=\"archive-meta\"><span>06 JUN 2026 · 8 PM PHT</span><span>Talk · Online</span></div><h2>Ancestral Wisdom in Modern Times: Indigenous Peoples as Guardians of Sustainable Ecosystems</h2><p class=\"archive-host\">Baganihan Collective</p><p class=\"archive-preview\">Eleonor V. Atencio shares a perspective rooted in indigenous knowledge, education and sustainable ecosystems.</p><details><summary>About this past event<span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></summary><div class=\"archive-details\"><p>Eleonor V. Atencio is a member of the Dumagat/Remontado ICCs/IPs of Brgy. Cuyambay, Tanay, Rizal. A public-school teacher and IPED Coordinator, she manages the School of Living Traditions of the Dumagat/Remontado known as Tukduan. She is currently President of Tanay Dumagat/Remontado Ancestral Domain Development Inc. (TANAYDRADDEVI) and is completing her Masters in Arts of Education Major in Indigenous Study.</p><p class=\"archive-closed\">This event has passed. Registration is closed.</p><a class=\"text-link\" href=\"/events/\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">Original event listing ↗<span class=\"visually-hidden\"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a></div></details></div></article></div><p class=\"editorial-note\">Original 3D illustrations inspired by the themes of these events. The Kabuohan story links to its published recap; the other records preserve the event listings.</p></section></main><footer class=\"site-footer\"><div class=\"footer-top\"><div class=\"footer-invitation\"><h2>Stay curious.<br/><span>Grow together.</span></h2><p>Rooted in the Philippines.<br/>Open to the world.</p></div><nav aria-label=\"Explore Mycelium\" class=\"footer-destinations\"><a class=\"footer-link\" href=\"/resources/\"><span>Browse Resources</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 12h16M13 5l7 7-7 7\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></path></svg></a><a class=\"footer-link\" href=\"/common-ground/\"><span>Explore the Forum</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 12h16M13 5l7 7-7 7\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></path></svg></a><a class=\"footer-link\" href=\"/videos/\"><span>Watch videos</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 12h16M13 5l7 7-7 7\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></path></svg></a><a class=\"footer-link\" href=\"/courses/\"><span>Find a course</span><svg aria-hidden=\"true\" fill=\"none\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\"><path d=\"M4 12h16M13 5l7 7-7 7\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"></p